<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="8.32" dur="5.359">Your Excellency, President Trump. Ladies</text><text start="10.96" dur="4.639">and gentlemen, good morning.</text><text start="13.679" dur="5.041">Mr. President, you arrived in Manila</text><text start="15.599" dur="6.241">just yesterday and already your schedule</text><text start="18.72" dur="5.52">has been packed to the hilt, which is</text><text start="21.84" dur="5.279">not exactly a surprise because we know</text><text start="24.24" dur="4.879">how hard you work. Last night, the first</text><text start="27.119" dur="4.4">lady and I had the pleasure of hosting</text><text start="29.119" dur="7.761">you and other leaders and their spouses</text><text start="31.519" dur="7.281">for the U Asan US special summit. I was</text><text start="36.88" dur="4.16">amazed to hear that in just a few hours</text><text start="38.8" dur="5.439">you had already held several substantive</text><text start="41.04" dur="5.199">meetings with other leaders and in a few</text><text start="44.239" dur="4.721">hours you and I will be departing</text><text start="46.239" dur="5.921">Manila. This time to go to the APEC</text><text start="48.96" dur="5.04">economic leaders meeting in Shenzhen.</text><text start="52.16" dur="4.239">Unfortunately, it means that you have</text><text start="54" dur="4.16">very little time here in Manila.</text><text start="56.399" dur="6.16">Fortunately, your brief stop here</text><text start="58.16" dur="7.039">includes a a a very highly condensed</text><text start="62.559" dur="7.681">version of the tour of the palace, but</text><text start="65.199" dur="7.041">it is uh some of the I was able to to to</text><text start="70.24" dur="4.32">recount to you some of the history that</text><text start="72.24" dur="4.72">has happened. This is a this is a very</text><text start="74.56" dur="6.16">much history has been made in this uh in</text><text start="76.96" dur="6.32">these buildings. Uh, not least of which</text><text start="80.72" dur="4.43">is that this year our two countries</text><text start="83.28" dur="2.479">commemorate 80 years of diplomatic</text><text start="85.15" dur="3.57">[snorts]</text><text start="85.759" dur="6.161">relations and 75 years of the</text><text start="88.72" dur="6.719">Philippines United States alliance under</text><text start="91.92" dur="6.64">the mutual defense treaty. But the ties</text><text start="95.439" dur="6.961">between our peoples go back well over a</text><text start="98.56" dur="7.28">century in various different forms. The</text><text start="102.4" dur="5.44">United States is our only treaty ally</text><text start="105.84" dur="5.44">and our relationship has continued to</text><text start="107.84" dur="5.52">grow and evolve over the many years. Now</text><text start="111.28" dur="4.879">we are also exploring new areas of</text><text start="113.36" dur="5.119">cooperation particularly in technology</text><text start="116.159" dur="5.201">where American leadership and innovation</text><text start="118.479" dur="4.721">continues to lead the way. We also see</text><text start="121.36" dur="4">tremendous opportunities to work most</text><text start="123.2" dur="5.119">more closely through American leadership</text><text start="125.36" dur="5.76">in super intelligence. And as we look to</text><text start="128.319" dur="5.761">the future, I am confident that we will</text><text start="131.12" dur="5.52">find new and important ways to deepen</text><text start="134.08" dur="4.799">our partnership.</text><text start="136.64" dur="5.28">However, since you&amp;#39;re strapped for time,</text><text start="138.879" dur="6">I thought a taste of Manila might be uh</text><text start="141.92" dur="6.88">might be good. So, last night I asked my</text><text start="144.879" dur="6.08">staff to um have some Jollibee delivered</text><text start="148.8" dur="5.2">as a late night snack for you and your</text><text start="150.959" dur="6.56">delegation. I think they gave you the um</text><text start="154" dur="7.12">Jollibee is a is a is a very uh very</text><text start="157.519" dur="6.561">popular chain and one of their main</text><text start="161.12" dur="5.52">products is uh fried chicken and we are</text><text start="164.08" dur="5.76">very proud to say that we have surpassed</text><text start="166.64" dur="6.16">KFC in the United States in terms of</text><text start="169.84" dur="5.84">popularity. So we thought that will give</text><text start="172.8" dur="4.88">you a taste of of of Manila and I think</text><text start="175.68" dur="5.12">may I hope some of your staff was also</text><text start="177.68" dur="5.6">able to partake. You have been working</text><text start="180.8" dur="5.28">very hard Mr. President. So just think</text><text start="183.28" dur="4.56">of it as uh providing extra energy for</text><text start="186.08" dur="4.32">all the work that you have to do that</text><text start="187.84" dur="5.6">you have done and continue to do and uh</text><text start="190.4" dur="5.119">that is in front of you. And so I uh</text><text start="193.44" dur="4.48">will not take too much of your time as I</text><text start="195.519" dur="4.881">know that our time is very short and we</text><text start="197.92" dur="4.72">have a great deal to go through uh</text><text start="200.4" dur="4.4">before we go to lunch. So Mr. President,</text><text start="202.64" dur="5.679">welcome. Thank you very much. And I want</text><text start="204.8" dur="5.6">to thank President Marcos, fantastic man</text><text start="208.319" dur="5.84">and a great friend of mine. We&amp;#39;ve known</text><text start="210.4" dur="6.32">each other for a long time. And uh I</text><text start="214.159" dur="5.201">very much appreciate your welcoming me</text><text start="216.72" dur="4.799">and us back to the Philippines as we</text><text start="219.36" dur="5.92">reaffirm one of America&amp;#39;s oldest and</text><text start="221.519" dur="6">most important alliances in the Pacific.</text><text start="225.28" dur="4.8">Generations of Americans and Filipino</text><text start="227.519" dur="5.841">patriots have served side by side and</text><text start="230.08" dur="5.439">formed a bond. And it&amp;#39;s a bond formed in</text><text start="233.36" dur="4.32">blood defending the sovereignty and</text><text start="235.519" dur="4.868">liberty of both of our nations. We&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="237.68" dur="4.08">been there together for a long time.</text><text start="240.387" dur="3.132">[snorts] Our people share common</text><text start="241.76" dur="3.44">history, common values, common</text><text start="243.519" dur="4.561">interests,</text><text start="245.2" dur="5.52">common architectural tastes. I love what</text><text start="248.08" dur="4.56">you&amp;#39;ve done here. Done a fantastic job.</text><text start="250.72" dur="4.32">But with this visit, we&amp;#39;re building on</text><text start="252.64" dur="4.8">these ties to make our partnership even</text><text start="255.04" dur="3.759">closer. Although I don&amp;#39;t imagine it can</text><text start="257.44" dur="3.359">get much closer because of the</text><text start="258.799" dur="4.881">relationship that we&amp;#39;ve had for a long</text><text start="260.799" dur="5.601">time. Our two nations along with Japan</text><text start="263.68" dur="4.64">recently launched the Luzon Economic</text><text start="266.4" dur="3.76">Corridor with the ultimate goal of</text><text start="268.32" dur="4.48">drawing 100 billion dollars of</text><text start="270.16" dur="4.56">investment from like-minded nations and</text><text start="272.8" dur="4.72">they&amp;#39;re coming one after another. As you</text><text start="274.72" dur="5.52">know, the critical industries and</text><text start="277.52" dur="4.959">economic security and the Philippines uh</text><text start="280.24" dur="4.239">will be there for a long period of time</text><text start="282.479" dur="3.921">and we&amp;#39;re with you all the way. There</text><text start="284.479" dur="4.16">are many other areas in which our two</text><text start="286.4" dur="5.6">nations can increase our collaboration</text><text start="288.639" dur="5.84">including energy security. We have more</text><text start="292" dur="6.08">energy than any country in the world by</text><text start="294.479" dur="6.401">double, even more than that. If you add</text><text start="298.08" dur="6.498">Russia and Saudi Arabia together, we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="300.88" dur="5.44">much bigger than those two combined.</text><text start="304.578" dur="4.542">[snorts] And then you add Venezuela,</text><text start="306.32" dur="4.96">which was our new acquisition.</text><text start="309.12" dur="4.639">It was an acquisition whether people</text><text start="311.28" dur="4.479">like to say that or not. And it&amp;#39;s been</text><text start="313.759" dur="4.641">amazing what happened to the United</text><text start="315.759" dur="4.321">States. But the United States is now the</text><text start="318.4" dur="4">world&amp;#39;s leading producer of oil and</text><text start="320.08" dur="4.559">natural gas by a lot. And we&amp;#39;ve just</text><text start="322.4" dur="4.32">announced a major new pipeline in Alaska</text><text start="324.639" dur="4.4">to export affordable, abundant supplies</text><text start="326.72" dur="5.199">of energy to our allies and friends</text><text start="329.039" dur="5.681">across the Pacific. And the Philippines</text><text start="331.919" dur="4.641">would be a very natural partner in this</text><text start="334.72" dur="4.88">effort. We&amp;#39;re working on that. You want</text><text start="336.56" dur="5.44">to use that. We have great energy and</text><text start="339.6" dur="4.24">great energy levels. We have it for</text><text start="342" dur="4.56">hundreds of years into the future. But</text><text start="343.84" dur="4.72">America&amp;#39;s civilian nuclear industry is</text><text start="346.56" dur="3.359">also the best and most advanced in the</text><text start="348.56" dur="3.84">world. And we&amp;#39;re dealing with you on</text><text start="349.919" dur="4.641">that. And for the Philippines to embrace</text><text start="352.4" dur="4.639">American technology in its first modern</text><text start="354.56" dur="5.52">nuclear project would underscore the</text><text start="357.039" dur="5.281">strength of the important relationship</text><text start="360.08" dur="4">and we&amp;#39;re going to probably do something</text><text start="362.32" dur="4.24">very big having to do with nuclear.</text><text start="364.08" dur="5.6">We&amp;#39;re very much into nuclear now that</text><text start="366.56" dur="5.68">it&amp;#39;s safe, powerful, and safe and</text><text start="369.68" dur="4.88">inexpensive. Working with President</text><text start="372.24" dur="4.72">Marcus, we&amp;#39;re also expanding our defense</text><text start="374.56" dur="4.96">cooperation, which has always been a key</text><text start="376.96" dur="4.959">pillar of security for this part of the</text><text start="379.52" dur="4.56">world. And since I took office, we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="381.919" dur="5.12">supported historic increases in foreign</text><text start="384.08" dur="5.28">military financing for the Philippines,</text><text start="387.039" dur="4.801">approve arm sales of over$5 billion</text><text start="389.36" dur="4.64">dollars. is we make the best armaments.</text><text start="391.84" dur="5.84">We make uh the best military equipment</text><text start="394" dur="8.96">in the world by far or whether you call</text><text start="397.68" dur="7.519">them uh I would say patriots thads. Uh</text><text start="402.96" dur="4.48">you could look at the defensive weapons</text><text start="405.199" dur="4.321">and you could look at the offensive</text><text start="407.44" dur="4.16">weapons is nobody makes weapons like we</text><text start="409.52" dur="4.32">do and we&amp;#39;re making them much faster.</text><text start="411.6" dur="5.12">We&amp;#39;re building 21 plants right now.</text><text start="413.84" dur="4.56">They&amp;#39;re expanding the industrial base,</text><text start="416.72" dur="4.319">the military industrial base is</text><text start="418.4" dur="4.16">expanding its capacity tremendously, so</text><text start="421.039" dur="4.72">you won&amp;#39;t have to wait so long when you</text><text start="422.56" dur="4.72">order. But we have uh the tomahawks. We</text><text start="425.759" dur="4.081">have everything there is to have.</text><text start="427.28" dur="4.96">Everybody wants it. And we only deal</text><text start="429.84" dur="4.16">with friends. We give it to friends. Not</text><text start="432.24" dur="3.359">a good idea selling good military</text><text start="434" dur="5.039">equipment to the enemy. We do have</text><text start="435.599" dur="5.281">enemies. But it&amp;#39;s uh the finest military</text><text start="439.039" dur="4.321">and finest we have the finest military</text><text start="440.88" dur="6">and military equipment anywhere in the</text><text start="443.36" dur="5.52">planet as you know we had a war you</text><text start="446.88" dur="4.159">could call it whatever it may be with</text><text start="448.88" dur="3.68">Venezuela that worked out very quickly.</text><text start="451.039" dur="4.16">Nobody killed. Think of it. Nobody</text><text start="452.56" dur="6.24">killed one day. Actually to be exact it</text><text start="455.199" dur="5.761">lasted for 48 minutes and was over. And</text><text start="458.8" dur="4.88">we&amp;#39;re doing very well in Iran to put it</text><text start="460.96" dur="4.799">mildly. They have no navy. They have no</text><text start="463.68" dur="4.959">air force. They have no nothing. But</text><text start="465.759" dur="4.961">America stands with the Filipino people</text><text start="468.639" dur="4.4">just as we have for generations. We&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="470.72" dur="4.8">been your ally, but not as close as it</text><text start="473.039" dur="4.961">is now. But we&amp;#39;ve been your ally. And</text><text start="475.52" dur="4.399">then you had some moments where that</text><text start="478" dur="3.759">alliance wasn&amp;#39;t very good during a</text><text start="479.919" dur="3.84">couple of administrations ago. It was</text><text start="481.759" dur="4.641">not a very good alliance. But our</text><text start="483.759" dur="4.401">alliance has never been better. And I</text><text start="486.4" dur="4.56">want to thank President Marcus once</text><text start="488.16" dur="5.84">again for hosting an outstanding ACSEAN</text><text start="490.96" dur="4.4">summit and a special dinner last night</text><text start="494" dur="4.639">with all the leaders throughout</text><text start="495.36" dur="5.04">Southeast Asia. We met with all of them</text><text start="498.639" dur="3.84">and uh they have great respect for you.</text><text start="500.4" dur="4">I have to tell you that and I do too.</text><text start="502.479" dur="4">And thank you very much for having us.</text><text start="504.4" dur="5.199">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you. Thank you. Thank you again,</text><text start="506.479" dur="4.881">Mr. President. So uh if you</text><text start="509.599" dur="3.841">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How concerned about how concerned are</text><text start="511.36" dur="4.64">you about the tensions in the West Phil</text><text start="513.44" dur="4.399">and if the Philines invoke the m</text><text start="516" dur="3.76">treaty. How ready are you?</text><text start="517.839" dur="3.921">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;m not concerned at all. I&amp;#39;m not</text><text start="519.76" dur="4.32">concerned about that at all. That&amp;#39;ll be</text><text start="521.76" dur="4.079">taken care of.</text><text start="524.08" dur="4.16">Any other questions? Any other</text><text start="525.839" dur="5.201">questions? Any other questions?</text><text start="528.24" dur="6.279">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, are you the only one to speak?</text><text start="531.04" dur="3.479">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Any other questions?</text><text start="536.24" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Again,</text><text start="536.72" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; the report.</text><text start="539.92" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Do you want to answer that?</text><text start="541.68" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; There&amp;#39;ll be no sign.</text><text start="544.64" dur="5.6">There is no signing.</text><text start="546.16" dur="6.08">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, no, the the the No, not not on not</text><text start="550.24" dur="5.68">on this trip. We are not doing we are</text><text start="552.24" dur="4.24">not covering that on this trip.</text><text start="555.92" dur="1.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr.</text><text start="556.48" dur="1.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much.</text><text start="557.44" dur="1.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you so much.</text><text start="558.08" dur="5">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you very much everybody.</text><text start="559.36" dur="3.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you ladies and gentle.</text><text start="572.56" dur="3.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Any other questions?</text></transcript>